\pard\intbl{\cf2 Free macros}\cell\pard\intbl{to the right of the matrix: four controls Macro 1-4, each moves any number of targets. Assign a target: right-click a control > Modulate with > Macro n (or a matrix row with source "Macro n"); amount, factor and offset per target. Curve per macro: Linear, Slow rise, Fast rise, S-curve. Each macro's targets are listed below it. Ideal for DAW automation: one lane moves many controls. Learning presets L35-L37.}\cell\pard\intbl{\cf4 yes (Macro 1..4, Macro 1..4 Curve)}\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph90\trleft0\clcbpat7\cellx2500\clcbpat7\cellx7300\clcbpat7\cellx10200
\pard\intbl{\cf2 Modulation matrix}\cell\pard\intbl{32 rows on four pages (buttons top right, in brackets: rows used; "Modulate with" in the right-click menu always takes the topmost free row). Each row: Source -> Target with Amount, Factor and Offset. The glowing display at the front pulses with the source. Note sources (Velocity, Note, Random per note, grain, filter and Osc1-3 envelope - each on its own -, LFOs with retrigger on note on/off) act per note: every voice has its own LFOs and its own values for grain controls, pitch, volume, oscillator, filter, all envelope times, Scan, filter contours and the LFO rates - a new note does not change the ones already sounding. Targets that exist only once (Echo, Reverb, EQ, Saturation, Width, master pan, Morph, Arp, Gate) follow the most recently played note; the row then shows 'global: last note'. The trash can at the end of a row clears the row (Ctrl+Z undoes it).}\cell\pard\intbl{\cf4 yes (all rows; Mod1..Mod32 Source, Target, Amount, Factor, Offset)}\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph90\trleft0\clcbpat8\cellx2500\clcbpat8\cellx7300\clcbpat8\cellx10200
\pard\intbl{\cf2 Glide / Time}\cell\pard\intbl{Portamento: notes glide into each other (Off / Always / Legato only), Time = glide duration.}\cell\pard\intbl{\cf4 yes (Glide, Glide time)}\cell\row
